## 5️⃣ State Management

### 5.1 Global Cart (Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// src/store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface CartItem {
  productId: string;
  quantity: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action: PayloadAction<CartItem>) {
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.productId === action.payload.productId);
      if (existing) existing.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      else state.items.push(action.payload);
    },
    removeItem(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter(i => i.productId !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

### 5.2 Persisting Cart

```ts
// src/store/index.ts
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import cartReducer from './cartSlice';
import storage from 'redux-persist/lib/storage';
import { persistReducer, persistStore } from 'redux-persist';

const persistConfig = {
  key: 'root',
  storage,
};

const persistedCart = persistReducer(persistConfig, cartReducer);

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: { cart: persistedCart },
});

export const persistor = persistStore(store);
```

Wrap your app with `<PersistGate>`.

---

## 6️⃣ API Integration

### 6.1 Axios Instance

```ts
// src/services/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL,
  timeout: 10000,
});

api.interceptors.request.use(config => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});

export default api;
```

### 6.2 Fetch Products (React Query)

```ts
// src/hooks/useProducts.ts
import { useQuery } from 'react-query';
import api from '../services/api';

export const useProducts = (page = 1) =>
  useQuery(['products', page], async () => {
    const { data } = await api.get('/products', { params: { page } });
    return data;
  });
```

---

## 7️⃣ Testing

| Layer | Tool | Sample Test |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Unit | Jest + React Testing Library | Test component renders correctly |
| Integration | React Testing Library | Test cart flow |
| End‑to‑End | Cypress | Simulate checkout |

**Example: Cart Button**

```tsx
// src/components/ui/AddToCartButton.test.tsx
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';
import { Provider } from 'react-redux';
import { store } from '../../store';
import { AddToCartButton } from './AddToCartButton';

test('adds item to cart', () => {
  render(
    <Provider store={store}>
      <AddToCartButton productId="123" />
    </Provider>
  );
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button'));
  const state = store.getState();
  expect(state.cart.items).toContainEqual({ productId: '123', quantity: 1 });
});
```

---

## 8️⃣ Deployment

| Platform | Pros | Typical Setup |
|----------|------|---------------|
| **Vercel** | Serverless, instant cache invalidation, preview URLs | `vercel --prod` |
| **Netlify** | Edge functions, split testing | `netlify deploy --prod` |
| **AWS Amplify** | Managed backend, CI/CD | Amplify Console |
| **Docker + ECS/EKS** | Full control | Dockerfile + ECS task definition |

### 8.1 CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
name: Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '20'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: amondnet/vercel-action@v20
        with:
          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
          alias-domains: 'www.yourshop.com'
```

---

## 9️⃣ Performance & SEO

| Technique | Why | How |
|-----------|-----|-----|
| **Code splitting** | Faster initial load | `React.lazy()` + `Suspense` |
| **Image optimization** | Reduce bandwidth | `next/image` or `react-image` |
| **Lazy loading** | Defer offscreen content | `loading="lazy"` |
| **SSR / SSG** | Crawlable pages | Next.js `getStaticProps` |
| **Structured data** | Rich snippets | JSON‑LD in `<Head>` |
| **Accessibility** | Inclusive UX | Semantic HTML, ARIA, keyboard nav |
| **Performance budgets** | Keep bundle size low | Bundle analyzer, Lighthouse |

---

## 🔑 Checklist Before Launch

- ✅ All core pages pass WCAG 2.1 AA
- ✅ Responsive across mobile, tablet, desktop
- ✅ Cart persists across sessions
- ✅ Payment gateway sandbox tested
- ✅ SEO meta tags, canonical URLs, robots.txt
- ✅ Analytics events wired
- ✅ Error boundaries & graceful degradation
- ✅ Security headers (CSP, HSTS)
- ✅ Load testing (k6, Loader.io)
- ✅ Backup & rollback plan

